==Other==

The eponymous {{Quarrel Falls}} fill the lower areas of the outpost with the peculiarly {{Fount Of Maguuma|regenerative waters}} of the {{Maguuma Jungle}}.

{{Sorrow's Furnace}} is a difficult {{explorable area}} under the {{Shiverpeak Mountains}}. It is considered by many to be the hardest PvE area in Guild Wars. The area contains the mining operations of the {{Stone Summit}} and is overrun with new types of Summit units. It is recommended if entering the Furnace for the first time to take on the quest "{{To Sorrow's Furnace}}" and its sub-quests as they present a primer to the area. 

'''Warning:''' Sorrow's Furnace is an underground area, with no map available, similar to {{The Catacombs}}, {{The Underworld}} and {{The Fissure of Woe}}. A map put together by fans is available from GameAmp [http://guildwars.gameamp.com/modules/game_map/game_map_images/164_full.jpg here].

''Tip:'' One of the best ways to explore this area (and avoid the disorientation due to the lack of a map) is to do the {{Summit Slaves}} quest. You will be able to enter as a spy and move about freely. This will allow you to know your way inside the Furnace, note the place of bosses and patrols as well as learn how to operate mechanisms.

