*Many of the NPCs in this city start many [[pre-Searing quest list|pre-searing quests]], especially the [[Academy training quests]].  It is also from Ascalon City that you can move your character to [[Ascalon City (Post-Searing)]]. But be aware that once you move on, there is no returning to pre-[[Searing]] Ascalon.
*Ironically, pre-Searing Ascalon City is actually considered an [[outpost]].
*King Adelbern (together with Ascalon Scribe) actually appears in two locations in the city at the same time. He can be seen with the Ascalon Scribe looking over the battle with the [[Charr]] and can also be seen on the staired peninsula on the northern side of the lake.
*It is possible to be killed by the Charr when watching their battle with the ascalon guard, but is a very rare happening.
*If you have a look at the large pond/reservoir off of Sir Tydus' right hand side, you may notice that it's somewhat familiar. Upon closer inspection, you will find that it is in fact the location of post-searing Ascalon City. Points of interest include:
**The stairway that leads into the water (the portal entrance sits atop these stairs in post-searing)
**The hill that sticks up out of the water in the back left corner (Tydus stands up there in post-searing)
**Looking beneath the water, you can see where all of the different NPCs will be in post-searing. The terrain changes slightly, but it's essentially the same.

